{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And I will send.</b> A term of sending forth." "<b>And it shall bereave you.</b> I have only a wild beast that bereaves — that is its way; a domestic animal that does not act thus, from where? Scripture says: ״וְשֵׁן בְּהֵמֹת אֲשַׁלַּח בָּם״ (Deuteronomy 32) — behold, two. And from where that it kills by its bite? Scripture says: ״עִם חֲמַת זֹחֲלֵי עָפָר״ (ibid.) — just as these bite and kill, so these bite and kill. There were already years in the Land of Israel: a donkey biting and killing, an עָרוֹד biting and killing." "<b>And it shall bereave you.</b> These are the small ones." "<b>And it shall cut off your livestock.</b> From outside." "<b>And it shall diminish you.</b> From inside." "<b>And your roads shall be desolate.</b> Great paths and small paths — here are seven punishments: the tooth of domesticated beast, the tooth of wild beast, the venom of crawling things, bereavement, cutting off, diminution, and desolation."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:45.553345557Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}